WEBVTT

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:15.370
The secret of hyper-speed flight which the Abh aim to control...

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:21.170
...lies in planar space in which physical laws differ from that of normal space.

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:28.970
As the term suggests, this space is comprised of two dimensions of space and the one dimension of time.

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:36.980
Abh interstellar spaceships travel through space enveloped in a spatial bubble which is separated from normal space.

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:48.050
The key to this other world, known as a saudec is a newly-discovered elementary particle called an uanon.

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:51.380
<i>Hey.</i>

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:52.760
<i>Tell me.</i>

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:54.140
<i>Am I...</i>

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.450
<i>a daughter of love?</i>

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:31.330
Frymec Négr

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:31.330
Daughter of Love

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:39.660
Jinto, look ahead.

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:40.630
What?!

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:46.700
Is that the Gosroth?

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.500
That's right.

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:51.270
It's a bit bigger than the Calike, isn't it?

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:16.220
Wow...

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.830
It's really incredible.

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:20.730
About time you noticed.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:24.730
Well, it's hard to tell from a distance, out here in space.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:28.740
You can because you've got your spatial sensor.

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:33.180
Don't look at me with that look of pity.

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:35.580
This is normal for me.

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:37.180
You're right.

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:41.250
Then I'll give you more time to take a look.

00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:43.820
I'd certainly appreciate that.

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:06.370
The Gosroth is the most advanced ship in the Empire.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:10.180
Its overall length is 12.82 üethdagh.

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:12.520
Is that all?

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:15.420
It's smaller than a front line battleship or transport...

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:20.060
...but you won't find another ship with more battle power...

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:23.430
...in the Empire, and in all of humanity.

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:26.030
I'm sure you're right.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.730
<i>What's wrong, trainee.</i>

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:31.670
<i>You can cut out the joyride.</i>

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:35.210
I wanted His Excellency...

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:38.910
...to see the difference between our shuttle and the patrol ship.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:40.610
<i>What do you mean?</i>

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:45.980
We're here.

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:47.220
Thank you.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.250
Just doing my job.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:53.530
Um...

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:55.220
Can I see you later?

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:58.000
The living quarters are limited.

00:04:58.270 --> 00:05:00.070
I'm sure we'll bump into each other again.

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:02.000
Well...

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:03.470
Next time then.

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:05.510
And thanks for bringing me here.

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:07.270
I had fun.

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.510
I'm glad.

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:30.430
I'm pleased to welcome you aboard, Your Excellency.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:32.760
I am commander of patrol ship Gosroth...

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:34.630
...Bomoüass Laicch.

00:05:35.570 --> 00:05:37.100
<i>What?</i>

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:40.630
<i>The Abh can introduce themselves properly.</i>

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:45.140
I am Linn Ssynec Rocr Ïarlucec Dreuc Haïder Ghintec

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:48.880
I'll be counting on you to get me to the capital.

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:52.880
You're in good hands.

00:05:58.090 --> 00:05:59.650
Prepare for departure!

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:02.220
All engines normal.

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:02.380
Supervisor

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:02.380
Chief Engineer Gyumuryua

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:05.220
Secretary

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:05.220
Chief Supply Officer Deesh

00:06:02.770 --> 00:06:04.930
Ship's pressure normal.

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:12.730
Senior Gunnery Officer

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:12.730
Advance-Guard Pilot Sariush

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:12.700
Flight preparations complete.

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:17.910
Approval from Bhorachr control...

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:18.230
Senior Operator

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:18.230
Advance-Guard Pilot Yunseryua

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:19.140
...to enter saudec received.

00:06:19.220 --> 00:06:24.200
Our permit gives us a window of 12 to 18 seconds after 15:27.

00:06:24.220 --> 00:06:27.100
Executive Officer and Senior Navigator

00:06:24.220 --> 00:06:27.100
Chief Pilot Lairia

00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:27.100
Ready for departure.

00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:28.450
Good.

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:30.590
Accelerate at 6 daimons.

00:06:31.930 --> 00:06:34.060
Head for Saudec Bhoracr.

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:39.130
Coming about to course 17-62-55.

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:39.960
Acknowledged.

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:57.440
Direction control complete.

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:00.690
Daïsairé!

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:19.740
All engines normal.

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:22.370
Three minutes to the saudec.

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:29.340
Generate space-time bubble!

00:07:30.520 --> 00:07:33.220
Space-time bubble generator stable!

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:37.550
Space-time bubble confirmed!

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:47.790
We're on our way to another dimension, aren't we?

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:49.170
That's right.

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:53.000
But you won't notice much difference on this spaceship.

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:55.010
There won't be any vibrations.

00:07:55.650 --> 00:07:58.580
The only difference will be a shift in color to a dull gray.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:00.780
One minute to the saudec.

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:04.590
Start count down from 30 seconds.

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:05.050
Aye-aye.

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:15.400
15...

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:17.070
14...

00:08:17.670 --> 00:08:18.500
13...

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:20.460
12...

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:21.940
11...

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:23.670
10...

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:25.400
9...

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:26.810
8...

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:28.380
7...

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:30.000
6...

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:31.410
5...

00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:33.070
4...

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:34.520
3...

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:36.180
2...

00:08:36.790 --> 00:08:37.880
1...

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:39.450
Entering.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:43.760
Confirm position.

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:50.090
Did you know that we are completely lost...

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:52.630
...as to our present location?

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:55.170
Huh? What do you mean?

00:08:56.740 --> 00:09:00.440
When converting from normal space to planar space

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:03.340
...we can only estimate our position...

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:05.140
...based on a theoretical probability.

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:09.910
Are you familiar with theoretical probabilities?

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:13.150
Another way of saying "random guess," right?

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:15.650
That's fairly accurate.

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:18.390
A saudec frequently presents...

00:09:18.460 --> 00:09:21.990
...incomplete spiral curves on the side of the planar space.

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:25.660
But we don't know what part of those curves we'll emerge from.

00:09:26.270 --> 00:09:28.100
Finished confirming position.

00:09:28.640 --> 00:09:29.970
On right shore...

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:31.440
...117 and 92 from threshold.

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:33.600
Acknowledged.

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:35.440
Bring up the planar image.

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:40.450
Positioned for transfer at 28 degrees.

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:45.840
Compute the route to our destination, Saudec Sfagnomr.

00:09:46.260 --> 00:09:47.690
Computations complete.

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:48.850
Acknowledged.

00:09:48.990 --> 00:09:50.690
I'll leave the rest to you, Lairia.

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:52.060
Get us on course.

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:53.460
Aye-aye.

00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:57.390
The rest of our operation will bore you...

00:09:57.470 --> 00:09:59.940
...even if it is your first time, Your Excellency.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:04.130
Um... I'm having trouble getting used to...

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:05.670
...that "Excellency" bit.

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:07.370
Why is that?

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:12.310
I have no idea how I should behave as a nobleman.

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:13.940
How to behave?

00:10:14.450 --> 00:10:17.650
Um, am I behaving strangely?

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:18.920
Strangely?

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:22.920
I mean, are lords expected to be arrogant and all?

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:26.250
Sometimes they're forgiven for being arrogant.

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:28.320
However...

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:31.530
...they don't always engender good will by being so.

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:33.190
Is that right.

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:35.530
Then my behavior isn't that strange.

00:10:36.810 --> 00:10:39.270
It's a lot better than being arrogant.

00:10:43.050 --> 00:10:44.740
You seem quite exhausted.

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:46.040
Not really...

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:49.080
Why don't I have someone show you to your room?

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:52.020
I'll ask the trainee that met you at the spaceport.

00:10:52.390 --> 00:10:54.450
Oh, her.

00:10:55.160 --> 00:10:56.750
Isn't she nobility too?

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:00.250
No.

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:02.060
That's strange.

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:04.900
She certainly seemed like the real thing.

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:06.760
Don't you know who she is?

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:11.400
Uh... Is she someone I should know about?

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:13.970
No.

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:17.670
Given your background, I can't expect you'd know about her.

00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:20.940
Flyer Trainee Abriel...

00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:22.210
...report to the bridge at once.

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:24.510
Abriel?!

00:11:26.260 --> 00:11:28.750
She's a princess of the Crybh family.

00:11:29.060 --> 00:11:32.760
She's the granddaughter of Her Majesty Empress Lamï.

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:36.260
The...

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:37.700
...imperial family.

00:11:41.540 --> 00:11:42.770
<i>Over the years...</i>

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:47.340
<i>...I'd gotten quite used to embarrassments.</i>

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:49.540
<i>But...</i>

00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:52.610
<i>...that was the first time...</i>

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:55.870
<i>...I'd ever faced such a huge embarrassment.</i>

00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:57.580
What's wrong, Jinto?

00:11:57.650 --> 00:11:59.480
You're being awfully quiet.

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:01.580
And why are you walking behind me?

00:12:03.190 --> 00:12:05.420
That's because, Your Imperial Highness...

00:12:11.670 --> 00:12:13.290
I'm not an Imperial Highness.

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:14.390
It's Royal Highness.

00:12:14.470 --> 00:12:17.500
My grandmother is the Empress, but my father is only a king.

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:20.730
Please forgive me, Your Royal Highness.

00:12:21.580 --> 00:12:24.440
If you insist on focusing on my relation to the Empress...

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:25.840
...call me lmperial Granddaughter.

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:27.540
...but that's not an official term.

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:30.810
"Your Highness Imperial Granddaughter" sounds stupid.

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:32.050
I suppose.

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:33.820
Uh, l mean... I agree, Your Highness.

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:35.050
Also...

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:39.030
...at birth, I was granted the title Bœrh Parhynr...

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:41.660
...and a domain to go with it.

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:45.530
So, at times, I'm referred to as Bœrh Parhynr.

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:49.590
Lately, I'm mostly referred to as Flyer Trainee Abriel.

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:51.100
However...

00:12:51.170 --> 00:12:53.610
...I thought I told you earlier.

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:56.640
That you shall call me Lafiel.

00:12:58.810 --> 00:13:01.650
So, friends call you Lafiel.

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:03.580
Not necessarily.

00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:06.280
None of my friends refer to me without a title.

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:07.910
Then, why?

00:13:09.190 --> 00:13:12.160
You were the first to ask me for my name.

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:16.260
It seems that as a granddaughter of the Empress...

00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:18.390
...I'm well-known and people know me and recognize me.

00:13:18.570 --> 00:13:21.900
They address me as "Your Royal Highness".

00:13:21.970 --> 00:13:24.240
Even my best friends call me "Your Highness".

00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:28.170
I kind of envy the other trainees at the institute...

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:30.080
...calling each other by their names.

00:13:31.210 --> 00:13:33.110
I'm sorry. I...

00:13:33.280 --> 00:13:34.840
It got worse...

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:38.720
...when I realized others weren't able to relax when I was around.

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:41.820
I'm really, sorry.

00:13:41.890 --> 00:13:43.590
There's nothing to be sorry about.

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:47.590
You've done nothing wrong, have you?

00:13:47.900 --> 00:13:50.330
You slipped up by calling me "Imperial Highness"...

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:52.330
...but it wasn't out of spite.

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:55.760
I wasn't brought up to tolerate disrespectful references...

00:13:55.840 --> 00:13:58.500
...but I shall accept any title if it is correct.

00:13:59.140 --> 00:14:02.870
So call me Royal Highness, Bœrh Parhynr...

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:05.140
...or whatever you wish, Your Excellency.

00:14:05.210 --> 00:14:07.270
No, I'd rather call you Lafiel.

00:14:07.350 --> 00:14:08.910
Don't get me wrong.

00:14:09.090 --> 00:14:12.540
I'm not insisting that you call me Lafiel.

00:14:12.760 --> 00:14:14.150
Please.

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:16.520
I want to call you Lafiel, and nothing else.

00:14:19.360 --> 00:14:21.230
You really don't have to.

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:23.790
But I really want to.

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:29.570
How about "lmperial Granddaughter"?

00:14:31.010 --> 00:14:32.470
What do I have to...

00:14:32.540 --> 00:14:35.410
What do I have to do for your forgiveness, Lafiel?!

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:43.850
I can sort of relate to that.

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:48.390
Because I was the only nobleman at my school.

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:55.390
This is your room here.

00:14:55.900 --> 00:14:58.090
I noticed from earlier...

00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:00.360
...but why are there so many paintings?

00:15:00.940 --> 00:15:02.630
They're just for decoration.

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:05.360
Wouldn't you agree that a warship needs some charm?

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:08.170
It just seems out of place.

00:15:08.580 --> 00:15:12.140
I'm sure there are pictures more suited to a spaceship.

00:15:12.210 --> 00:15:15.380
What feelings do you get from looking at these?

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:18.080
What do you mean?

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:19.550
Well...

00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:23.150
...you've never seen real sunflowers, right?

00:15:23.230 --> 00:15:25.130
Sure I've seen sunflowers.

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:27.090
The capital does have a botanical garden...

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:29.060
...and our residence has its own flower garden.

00:15:29.130 --> 00:15:30.190
I see.

00:15:30.270 --> 00:15:32.060
Then, how about this one?

00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:35.540
I'm sure I've never seen anything like it.

00:15:36.070 --> 00:15:37.800
What does it look like to you?

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:39.500
Let's see.

00:15:39.610 --> 00:15:41.840
Like a scene from a dream.

00:15:42.340 --> 00:15:44.210
Of a place that doesn't exist in reality?

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:45.410
No, not really.

00:15:45.480 --> 00:15:49.010
I know that we originally came from places like this.

00:15:49.350 --> 00:15:51.750
Like a home abandoned?

00:15:52.560 --> 00:15:55.290
Space is our home now.

00:15:57.060 --> 00:15:59.050
We are the only citizens of space...

00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:01.190
...and we're very proud of that.

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:06.830
How does that picture look to you, Jinto?

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:09.100
Is that a scene that's common on land?

00:16:09.170 --> 00:16:10.370
No.

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:13.970
Scenery like that is rare even in surface worlds.

00:16:14.710 --> 00:16:16.440
Then how does it look to you?

00:16:24.350 --> 00:16:26.480
Whenever I see a blue sky like that...

00:16:26.560 --> 00:16:28.490
...I remember my dead mother.

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:34.220
I was told when I was a kid that my mother left for the skies.

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:35.620
Mother?

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:40.230
But I thought you were the son of a father.

00:16:40.300 --> 00:16:43.070
Aren't you the son of His Excellency Dreuc Haïder?

00:16:43.210 --> 00:16:44.730
Well, yes I am...

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:48.040
Oh, I get it!

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:50.870
You've heard of a system called marriage, haven't you?

00:16:50.950 --> 00:16:51.970
I have!

00:16:52.180 --> 00:16:53.110
I see.

00:16:53.180 --> 00:16:55.740
What is it like to have two parents?

00:16:56.290 --> 00:16:59.650
Were you sad when your mother died?

00:16:59.960 --> 00:17:00.850
Sure...

00:17:01.360 --> 00:17:02.790
...I was devastated.

00:17:06.260 --> 00:17:07.890
You must forgive me.

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:10.360
That question was inappropriate.

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:12.700
No, it's okay.

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:17.370
I don't remember too well, since I was really little then.

00:17:18.610 --> 00:17:22.070
Although I do remember the parents who brought me up.

00:17:24.110 --> 00:17:27.910
But that way, you can't possibly have any birth secrets.

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:30.550
Birth secrets?

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:33.020
What makes you say that?

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:36.150
I had a birth secret.

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:39.530
I didn't know whether I was a daughter of love.

00:17:39.860 --> 00:17:41.490
Wouldn't that worry you?

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:43.920
A daughter of love?

00:17:46.070 --> 00:17:47.630
What's that?

00:17:48.370 --> 00:17:49.390
Don't you know about it?

00:17:51.370 --> 00:17:55.870
There's a lot we weren't taught in the classes I attended.

00:17:56.450 --> 00:17:58.070
Do you know how Abh are born?

00:17:58.150 --> 00:17:58.810
Huh?

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:01.170
Well...

00:18:01.250 --> 00:18:05.280
I do know that it's not through conception in a human body.

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:07.480
Sometimes we do it that way.

00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:09.520
But...

00:18:09.860 --> 00:18:11.290
...what about the gene exam?

00:18:11.590 --> 00:18:13.620
First, the fertilized egg is extracted from the body.

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:15.990
In most cases, it's transferred to an artificial uterus...

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:18.260
...but some women decide to return the egg to...

00:18:18.330 --> 00:18:20.930
...their own uterus for the unique experience.

00:18:21.540 --> 00:18:22.770
I see.

00:18:23.770 --> 00:18:24.970
But...

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:27.910
...it is true that conception normally takes place artificially.

00:18:29.140 --> 00:18:33.880
To us, it seems like all you Abhs have birth secrets.

00:18:34.350 --> 00:18:36.440
I did learn about it...

00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:38.920
...but there were all sorts of ridiculous information.

00:18:38.990 --> 00:18:39.610
Like what?

00:18:40.720 --> 00:18:41.350
Well...

00:18:41.420 --> 00:18:44.360
...like cloning yourself to make your own child...

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:47.050
...or mixing the genes of a complete stranger...

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:50.960
...or combining same-sex genes with that of your own.

00:18:51.030 --> 00:18:52.020
Also...

00:18:52.100 --> 00:18:54.730
...that other person could be a relative in some cases.

00:18:55.300 --> 00:18:57.140
How can you think of such...

00:18:57.210 --> 00:18:58.170
We do all of those things.

00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:01.710
Everyone should be free to do as he or she wishes.

00:19:01.810 --> 00:19:02.800
However...

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:07.610
...having said that, the most natural way to produce a child...

00:19:07.680 --> 00:19:11.680
...is to combine your genes with the genes of the person you love.

00:19:12.760 --> 00:19:14.950
I'm relieved to hear you say that.

00:19:15.520 --> 00:19:18.580
To ask someone that you want their genes...

00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:21.930
...is the ultimate way to express your love for that person.

00:19:27.070 --> 00:19:29.560
And children born as a result of this...

00:19:29.640 --> 00:19:30.730
I get it!

00:19:30.810 --> 00:19:32.360
Daughter of love, right?

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:33.100
Right.

00:19:33.180 --> 00:19:36.110
Or the son of love, if the child is a boy.

00:19:36.180 --> 00:19:39.310
Then, why don't you ask...

00:19:39.380 --> 00:19:40.910
...your father directly?

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:43.280
Or, has your father...?

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:47.620
Oh, my father's still alive.

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:51.150
He should be up and around for another 200 years.

00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:54.330
Is that what you were assuming?

00:19:54.800 --> 00:19:55.960
Yeah, sort of.

00:19:56.030 --> 00:19:58.470
Then why don't you ask him?

00:19:58.530 --> 00:20:00.090
I did ask him, actually.

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:02.400
But my father wouldn't tell me.

00:20:02.600 --> 00:20:04.730
He said that one's character...

00:20:04.810 --> 00:20:07.780
...becomes richer when you have a birth secret.

00:20:10.650 --> 00:20:12.140
It's no laughing matter.

00:20:12.210 --> 00:20:14.480
Sorry. Can't you check into it?

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:16.550
The regulations state that...

00:20:16.620 --> 00:20:20.350
...my genetic records can't be released to me until I'm an adult.

00:20:20.420 --> 00:20:21.480
Is that so.

00:20:21.560 --> 00:20:24.150
My father was teasing me.

00:20:24.230 --> 00:20:25.280
What?

00:20:25.360 --> 00:20:28.760
I kept bugging him about who supplied my genes...

00:20:29.570 --> 00:20:32.800
...so one day he told me he was bringing her home.

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:38.270
Here's the other half of your origin. Holia!

00:20:46.010 --> 00:20:47.570
She was the cat we owned!

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:55.720
You didn't actually believe that, did you?

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:59.460
What do you expect? I was only 8 years old.

00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:01.930
I cried all night.

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:04.630
And you can't imagine how anxious I became.

00:21:05.270 --> 00:21:09.100
I'd wonder if my palms would start to swell and become paws.

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:12.670
Or if I'd start growing cat claws.

00:21:13.240 --> 00:21:16.180
Or if the shape of my eyes would change.

00:21:21.580 --> 00:21:23.740
Holia was a great cat...

00:21:23.950 --> 00:21:27.790
...but I couldn't stand thinking that she was half of me.

00:21:27.860 --> 00:21:29.820
What I really couldn't stand...

00:21:29.890 --> 00:21:34.090
...was the thought of my father having his child with a cat.

00:21:37.530 --> 00:21:38.590
Stop laughing!

00:21:40.470 --> 00:21:41.730
Sorry.

00:21:41.800 --> 00:21:44.640
You don't believe that story anymore, right?

00:21:46.040 --> 00:21:46.870
Right.

00:21:48.710 --> 00:21:52.170
But I still remember those anxious days.

00:21:52.780 --> 00:21:56.510
My main reason for joining the military so early...

00:21:56.590 --> 00:21:59.320
...was because I wanted to get away from my father.

00:21:59.660 --> 00:22:01.250
Do you dislike your father?

00:22:02.520 --> 00:22:03.890
I don't dislike him.

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:06.390
I love him, and I'm very proud of him.

00:22:07.160 --> 00:22:09.150
It's just that, when I'm near him...

00:22:09.230 --> 00:22:11.290
...he can be quite irritating.

00:22:15.870 --> 00:22:16.800
So...

00:22:16.870 --> 00:22:19.240
...I noticed you've been speaking in the past tense.

00:22:19.680 --> 00:22:21.300
Did he finally tell you who she was?

00:22:22.880 --> 00:22:25.140
She's a woman that I know quite well.

00:22:27.120 --> 00:22:30.140
I know now that I'm a daughter of love.

00:22:33.760 --> 00:22:35.190
I'm glad for you.

00:22:41.000 --> 00:22:42.160
<i>At that time...</i>

00:22:43.070 --> 00:22:45.030
<i>...we had absolutely no idea...</i>

00:22:45.100 --> 00:22:47.900
<i>...that a long, long war...</i>

00:22:47.970 --> 00:22:49.700
<i>...was about to begin.</i>

00:23:02.890 --> 00:23:04.990
The United Mankind.

00:24:30.660 --> 00:24:32.880
Now, go on.

00:24:40.720 --> 00:24:41.550
Lafiel...

00:24:46.950 --> 00:24:48.340
Nothing yet?

00:24:48.610 --> 00:24:49.220
Quiet.

00:24:57.170 --> 00:24:59.860
Déucrémhoth

00:24:57.170 --> 00:24:59.860
Next episode

00:24:57.170 --> 00:24:59.860
Surprise Attack
